{"t": 1793708241.852702, "s": 0.08, "code": "import numpy as np\n# W_proj shape (384,1536): rows=resid dim, cols=mlp neurons. Row norm = write strength to that dim.\n# W_o shape (384,384): rows? Actually W_o stored (out=384,in=384)? Wait split columns for heads. Rows=resid out dim. So row norm = write strength.\n# W_fc shape (1536,384): rows=mlp neurons, cols=resid in. Col norm = read strength from resid dim? Actually fc reads resid: out=1536, in=384. So column norm per resid dim = read strength.\nfor layer in [0,1,2,3]:\n    Wproj=W[f'W_proj.{layer}']  # (384,1536)\n    Wo=W[f'W_o.{layer}']  # (384,384)\n    Wfc=W[f'W_fc.{layer}']  # (1536,384)\n    for dim in [21,99,184]:\n        proj_row_norm=float(np.linalg.norm(Wproj[dim,:]))\n        o_row_norm=float(np.linalg.norm(Wo[dim,:]))\n        fc_col_norm=float(np.linalg.norm(Wfc[:,dim]))\n        print(f\"L{layer} dim{dim} proj_row {proj_row_norm:.2f} o_row {o_row_norm:.2f} fc_col {fc_col_norm:.2f}\")\n    print(\"---\")\n", "out": "L0 dim21 proj_row 5.17 o_row 6.04 fc_col 1.42\nL0 dim99 proj_row 2.31 o_row 3.90 fc_col 2.32\nL0 dim184 proj_row 8.56 o_row 2.17 fc_col 1.89\n---\nL1 dim21 proj_row 1.31 o_row 0.42 fc_col 2.24\nL1 dim99 proj_row 1.33 o_row 1.12 fc_col 2.27\nL1 dim184 proj_row 5.78 o_row 2.77 fc_col 3.05\n---\nL2 dim21 proj_row 2.03 o_row 1.13 fc_col 3.30\nL2 dim99 proj_row 2.82 o_row 1.73 fc_col 2.40\nL2 dim184 proj_row 5.83 o_row 3.25 fc_col 3.21\n---\nL3 dim21 proj_row 8.19 o_row 10.13 fc_col 3.52\nL3 dim99 proj_row 4.19 o_row 3.88 fc_col 3.59\nL3 dim184 proj_row 13.49 o_row 3.96 fc_col 2.69\n---\n"}
